{
  "date": "2026-10-21T20:00:56+00:00",
  "hypothesis": "Overnight effect: buy Micron (MU) at every close and sell at the next day's open, every trading day",
  "sources": [],
  "result": {
    "traded_ticker": "MU",
    "total_return": 1.3208247121710595,
    "buy_and_hold_return": 25.967282763118163,
    "spy_same_days_return": 3.6517467574631794,
    "spy_random_days_return": 4.472090744816599,
    "time_in_market": 0.9996630727762803,
    "sharpe": 0.38082627954738835,
    "max_drawdown": -0.720039231257813,
    "n_trades": 2967
  },
  "explanation": "\n\nThe overnight‑only “buy at close, sell at next open” rule on Micron generated a cumulative gain of about +132 % over the period, far below the +2 596 % you would have earned by simply holding MU and also lagging the S&P 500’s +365 % return on the same trading days. The strategy’s Sharpe ratio of 0.38 and a maximum drawdown of –72 % indicate modest risk‑adjusted performance and considerable volatility. No robustness checks were reported, so there is no evidence to suggest the observed edge is anything more than random luck. Verdict: **Weak**.",
  "code": "import yfinance as yf\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\ndef download_with_retry(ticker, start):\n    for attempt in range(3):\n        df = yf.download(ticker, start=start, auto_adjust=True, progress=False)\n        if df is not None and not df.empty:\n            return df\n        time.sleep(3)\n    raise Exception(f\"Failed to download data for {ticker} after 3 attempts\")\n\n# Hypothesis: Buy MU at close, sell at next open. Data: Open, Close. Supported by yfinance.\ntraded_ticker = \"MU\"\nstart_date = \"2015-01-01\"\n\n# Download traded asset\ndf = download_with_retry(traded_ticker, start_date)\nclose = df[\"Close\"].squeeze()\nopen_ = df[\"Open\"].squeeze()\n\n# Align data: need Close_t and Open_{t+1}\n# overnight_ret_t = Open_{t+1} / Close_t - 1\n# This return is realized on date_{t+1}\nclose_t = close.iloc[:-1]\nopen_t1 = open_.iloc[1:].values\ndates_t1 = close.index[1:]\n\novernight_ret = (open_t1 / close_t.values) - 1\nstrat_ret = pd.Series(overnight_ret - 0.001, index=dates_t1)  # 0.1% round-trip cost per entry\n\n# Holding series: 1 on every day we enter a trade (every day except last)\nholding = pd.Series(1, index=close.index[:-1])\nposition = holding.shift(1)  # Not used directly for returns but follows convention\n\nn_trades = len(strat_ret)\ntotal_return = (1 + strat_ret).prod() - 1\n\n# Buy and Hold Return on traded asset over same period (first close to last close)\nbuy_and_hold_return = (close.iloc[-1] / close.iloc[0]) - 1\n\n# Download SPY for benchmarks\nspy_df = download_with_retry(\"SPY\", start_date)\nspy_close = spy_df[\"Close\"].squeeze()\n\n# Align SPY to strategy dates (dates_t1)\nspy_close_aligned = spy_close.reindex(dates_t1).ffill()  # Use ffill for missing SPY days (holidays)\nspy_daily_ret_full = spy_close.pct_change().dropna()\nspy_daily_ret_strat_dates = spy_close_aligned.pct_change().dropna()\n\n# spy_same_days_return: compounded SPY return over only the days the strategy held a position\nspy_same_days_return = (1 + spy_daily_ret_strat_dates).prod() - 1\n\n# spy_random_days_return: (1 + mean daily SPY return over full period) ** n_trades - 1\nspy_mean_daily_ret = spy_daily_ret_full.mean()\nspy_random_days_return = (1 + spy_mean_daily_ret) ** n_trades - 1\n\n# Sharpe: annualize with sqrt(252) (not crypto)\nrisk_free = 0.0\nann_factor = np.sqrt(252)\nsharpe = (strat_ret.mean() - risk_free) / strat_ret.std() * ann_factor if strat_ret.std() > 0 else 0.0\n\n# Equity curve for strategy\nstrat_equity = (1 + strat_ret).cumprod()\n\n# Max Drawdown\nrunning_max = strat_equity.cummax()\ndrawdown = strat_equity / running_max - 1\nmax_drawdown = drawdown.min()\n\n# Time in market: fraction of days strategy held a position (holding == 1) relative to traded asset calendar\ntime_in_market = holding.sum() / len(close)\n\n# Prepare equity.csv: date, strategy, spy (buy-and-hold SPY starting 1.0 on first strategy date)\nfirst_strat_date = strat_equity.index[0]\nspy_equity_aligned = spy_close_aligned / spy_close_aligned.loc[first_strat_date]\n\nequity_df = pd.DataFrame({\n    'date': strat_equity.index,\n    'strategy': strat_equity.values,\n    'spy': spy_equity_aligned.values\n})\nequity_df.to_csv(\"equity.csv\", index=False)\n\n# Result JSON\nresult = {\n    \"traded_ticker\": traded_ticker,\n    \"total_return\": float(total_return),\n    \"buy_and_hold_return\": float(buy_and_hold_return),\n    \"spy_same_days_return\": float(spy_same_days_return),\n    \"spy_random_days_return\": float(spy_random_days_return),\n    \"time_in_market\": float(time_in_market),\n    \"sharpe\": float(sharpe),\n    \"max_drawdown\": float(max_drawdown),\n    \"n_trades\": int(n_trades)\n}\n\nprint(f'RESULT {json.dumps(result)}')\n",
